Then you notice the pigeons. Dozens of them—normally restless, fluttering, pecking at crumbs. Now they’re frozen mid-flight. Wings spread, beaks open. Silent. Waiting.

A vendor drops a loaf of bread. It doesn’t fall. It *hovers. One inch above the ground. Dust motes swirl around it like tiny galaxies caught in slow motion.

